# src/custom

Your code. neucli never writes, changes or deletes anything in this folder.

Generated code lives in `src/neucli/` and is rewritten on every `neucli generate`.
Don't edit it: neucli skips files you edited (with a warning) instead of
overwriting them, so your config and the code drift apart.

To use your own React component from the config, put it here and point a
component at it:

```yaml
components:
  Pricing:
    file: ./custom/Pricing.tsx   # relative to src/
    props:
      plan: text
pages:
  - path: /
    name: Home
    sections:
      - type: Pricing
        props: { plan: Pro }
```

The file needs a default export. It receives the declared props, `children`,
and `className` (sizing, fill, color and border set on the instance arrive as
classes there).
